{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Fash Mosque (Arabic: مسجد الفسح‎ ‎ ), or Masjid Uhud is a small mosque beneath the Mount Uhud, under the cave, in Medina, Saudi Arabia.","title":"Fas'h mosque"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" There are some accounts of the Islamic prophet Muhammad fulfilling the Zuhr prayer on the day of the Battle of Uhud after the battle.","title":"Fas'h mosque"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Initial construction was already destroyed and there are only few remnants of the east, west and south wall, and the mihrab mujawwaf which is still visible.","title":"Fas'h mosque"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The building is now surrounded by an iron fence to guard its sustainability.","title":"Fas'h mosque"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It is 4.5 km from Al-Masjid an-Nabawi.","title":"Fas'h mosque"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Burj Pukhta or Burj Pukta (Punjabi: ਬੁਰ੍ਜ ਪੁਖਤਾ ) is a village in Phillaur tehsil of Jalandhar District of Punjab State, India.","title":"Burj Pukhta"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located 3.3 km away from Nagar, 47.7 km from Jalandhar and 115 km from state capital Chandigarh.","title":"Burj Pukhta"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Burj Pukhta has postal head office in Phillaur which is 4.5 km away from the village.","title":"Burj Pukhta"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The village is administrated by a sarpanch who is an elected representative of village as per Panchayati raj (India).","title":"Burj Pukhta"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Yakkala is a township located on Colombo-Kandy Highway (A1), 30 km away from Colombo, Sri Lanka.","title":"Yakkala"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It forms part of Gampaha Municipal Council and belongs to Gampaha District, Western Province.","title":"Yakkala"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Its elevation is 30m above MSL.","title":"Yakkala"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Distances from Yakkala to main cities are; 30 km to Colombo(A1), 86 km to Kandy(A1), 4.5 km to Gampaha(A33) and 13 km to Radawana(B479).","title":"Yakkala"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rathsoon or Rathsun is a village in the Beerwah tehsil of the Budgam district in Jammu and Kashmir, India.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The village population is over 7,500, being one of the largest in tehsil Beerwah.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Rathsoon has a shrine of one Sofi Saint Baab Sahab, located on the hill top.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The neighboring village is Aripanthan, these two villages are separated by River Stream( Nallah) Sukhnag.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The village is 27 km away from Srinagar.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The nearest town is Magam, 4.5 km away.","title":"Rathsoon"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Damerdash Mosque (Arabic: مسجد الدمرداش‎ ‎ ) is a historical mosque originally built during the Abbasid era, in Cairo, Egypt.","title":"Demerdash Mosque"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located near Damerdash Hospital which belongs to the Ain Shams University Faculty of Medicine.","title":"Demerdash Mosque"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Mosque of Abu Dahab is a mosque in Cairo, Egypt just beside Al Azhar Mosque.","title":"Muhammad Bek Abu El Dahab Complex"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The mosque was built by the Amir Mohamed Beh Abu El Dahab, one of the leaders of Egypt during the rule of the Ottoman Empire.","title":"Muhammad Bek Abu El Dahab Complex"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is located in Al Azhar Street, beside the main entrance of the Azhar Mosque and it is the fourth mosque in Egypt to be built according to the Ottoman style of architecture.","title":"Muhammad Bek Abu El Dahab Complex"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It was originally built as a Madrasa to host the number of students that were coming to study in the Azhar University.","title":"Muhammad Bek Abu El Dahab Complex"}],"peer_messages":["soon"}
